      "geometry": "rect",
      "text": "Part 1: Public Dataset (Base Training): To ensure the ML model (Random Forest/XGBoost) learns a wide variety of attack signatures, it is initially trained on a modern, standard dataset WUSTL-EHLL (specifically containing medical network attacks). This provides the model with a robust baseline of hundreds of thousands of threat interactions.\n\nPart 2: Custom Dataset Generation (Live Validation): Instead of relying purely on offline data, a custom dataset is actively generated. The custom Python honeypot running on the Raspberry Pi is subjected to simulated, controlled attacks (e.g., Nmap scans, Hydra brute-force, DoS) using Kali Linux. The resulting live network traffic is captured as .pcap files and converted into statistical features.",
